What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/nanokvm-go-expansion/<device>/mode
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.4
Contact:	Cocoa <i@uwucocoa.moe>
Description:
		(RW) What the two lines of the auxiliary USB-C port are, one
		of the names in "modes":

		========  ===================================================
		off       both inputs, pulled down: the mode at boot
		uart      the UART, TXD on line 0 and RXD on line 1
		gpio      both GPIOs, for userspace
		pwm       both PWM outputs, for userspace
		pwm-gpio  line 0 a PWM output, line 1 a GPIO
		gpio-pwm  line 0 a GPIO, line 1 a PWM output
		i2c       a bit-banged I2C bus, SDA on line 0 and SCL on
		          line 1, both pulled up
		========  ===================================================

		The GPIOs and PWM channels a mode does not hand to
		userspace stay requested by the driver, the GPIOs as inputs
		and the PWM channels disabled. Writing a mode fails with
		EBUSY while userspace still holds a GPIO or a PWM channel
		that the new mode takes back.

